  "dom_id": "step-q341492",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X\u223cN(1.5,{\\sigma }^{2})$ and $P(X<2)=0.5910,$ use the table value to find ${\\sigma }^{2},$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ | $\\,0.04\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.5478\\,$ | $\\,0.5517\\,$ | $\\,0.5557\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.5871\\,$ | $\\,0.5910\\,$ | $\\,0.5948\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.6255\\,$ | $\\,0.6293\\,$ | $\\,0.6331\\,$ |\n\n${\\sigma }^{2}\u2248$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, we convert the given probability into a cumulative probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<2)=0.5910\\,\u21d2\\,P(X\\le 2)=0.5910\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we transform to a standard normal random variable by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2) & =0.5910 \\\\ P\\,(Z\\le \\frac{2-1.5}{\\sigma }) & =0.5910 \\\\ \u03a6\\,(\\frac{0.5}{\\sigma }) & =0.5910 \\\\ \\frac{0.5}{\\sigma } & ={\u03a6}^{-1}(0.5910)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to the table, we have\n\n$$\n\u03a6(0.23)=0.5910\\,\u21d2\\,{\u03a6}^{-1}(0.5910)=0.23.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{0.5}{\\sigma } & =0.23 \\\\ \\sigma  & =\\frac{0.5}{0.23} \\\\ \\sigma  & \u22482.173\\,91,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $5$ decimal places.\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2}=(2.173\\,91)^{2}\u22484.73.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
